Okay, here is a quick reference flowchart for adult Diabetic Ketoacidosis (DKA) management. This is a simplified overview and should **always** be used in conjunction with institutional protocols and clinical judgment.

**DKA Management Flowchart (Adult)**

```mermaid
graph TD
    A[Suspected DKA] --> B{Confirm DKA};
    B -- Yes --> C[Initial Assessment & Labs];
    B -- No --> Z[Treat Underlying Cause / Alternative Diagnosis];

    C --> D[IV Fluids (Isotonic Saline)];
    C --> E[Insulin Therapy (IV)];
    C --> F[Electrolyte Monitoring];

    D --> G{Fluid Resuscitation};
    G -- Initial --> H[0.9% NaCl @ 1-1.5 L/hr];
    H --> I{Reassess Volume Status};
    I -- Improved --> J[Switch to 0.45% NaCl];
    I -- Poor --> K[Continue 0.9% NaCl];
    J --> L{Monitor Urine Output};
    L -- Adequate --> M[Adjust Fluid Rate];
    L -- Inadequate --> K;
    M --> N{Corrected Sodium > 145};
    N -- Yes --> O[Switch to 0.45% NaCl];
    N -- No --> P[Continue 0.45% NaCl];
    P --> Q{Fluid Goal Reached?};
    Q -- No --> M;
    Q -- Yes --> R[Stop IV Fluids];

    E --> S{Insulin Bolus? (Controversial)};
    S -- Yes --> T[0.1 U/kg IV Regular Insulin];
    S -- No --> U[Start Insulin Infusion];
    T --> U[Start Insulin Infusion];
    U --> V[0.1 U/kg/hr IV Regular Insulin];
    V --> W{Monitor Glucose};
    W -- Glucose > 250 mg/dL --> X[Continue Infusion];
    W -- Glucose < 250 mg/dL --> Y[Add D5W to Fluids];
    Y --> Z1{Monitor Glucose};
    Z1 -- Glucose 200-250 mg/dL --> AA[Continue Infusion];
    Z1 -- Glucose < 200 mg/dL --> BB[Stop Insulin Infusion];
    X --> W;
    AA --> W;
    BB --> CC[Check Anion Gap & Bicarb];

    F --> DD[Initial Labs];
    DD --> EE[K+ < 3.3 mEq/L];
    EE -- Yes --> FF[Hold Insulin, Give K+];
    FF --> GG[Recheck K+];
    GG -- K+ > 3.3 --> U;
    GG -- K+ < 3.3 --> FF;
    EE -- No --> HH[K+ 3.3 - 5.2];
    HH --> U;
    HH --> II[Monitor K+ q2-4h];
    II --> JJ[K+ < 3.3];
    JJ -- Yes --> FF;
    JJ -- No --> U;

    CC --> KK{Anion Gap Normal & Bicarb > 15-18};
    KK -- Yes --> LL[Transition to Subcutaneous Insulin];
    KK -- No --> MM[Continue IV Insulin & Fluids];
    MM --> CC;

    LL --> NN[Overlap SC & IV Insulin];
    NN --> OO[SC Insulin: 0.1-0.2 U/kg q6-8h];
    OO --> PP[Stop IV Insulin];
    PP --> QQ[Monitor Glucose & Ketones];
    QQ --> RR[Adjust SC Insulin];
    RR --> SS[Discharge Planning / Education];

    subgraph Initial Labs
        direction LR
        DD1[Glucose]
        DD2[Electrolytes (Na, K, Cl, Phos, Mg)]
        DD3[Bicarb/Venous pH]
        DD4[Anion Gap]
        DD5[Ketones (Serum/Urine)]
        DD6[BUN/Cr]
        DD7[CBC]
        DD8[ECG]
    end

    subgraph Fluid Regimen
        direction TB
        F1[Initial: 0.9% NaCl 1-1.5 L/hr]
        F2[After Resuscitation/Corrected Na > 145: 0.45% NaCl]
        F3[If K+ < 3.3: Hold Insulin, Give K+]
        F4[Monitor Urine Output]
        F5
